WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.520
Child stars live unique lives that frequently&nbsp;
include tons of money. While there are plenty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.840
of cautionary tales of kid actors who've&nbsp;
struggled with demons, there are others who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:14.080
turned out just fine, like the following&nbsp;
ones who ended up with loads of cash.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:19.760
You might only be aware of Kaley Cuoco from&nbsp;
her work on the wildly popular sitcom The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:24.880
Big Bang Theory, but she's been kicking around&nbsp;
Hollywood since she was just seven years old.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:31.120
Her first big breakout came in 2002 when she&nbsp;
played Bridget on the ABC sitcom 8 Simple Rules,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:36.800
but it was her performance as Penny on Big Bang&nbsp;
that made her a supernova. And you don't star on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:42.480
one of TV's most-watched shows for over a decade&nbsp;
without making some serious cash along the way.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:48.800
Cuoco reportedly started out earning around&nbsp;
$45,000 per Big Bang episode. This number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.880
increased as the show gained a bigger and&nbsp;
bigger audience. For the final two seasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:58.240
she and her co-stars were all making $1 million&nbsp;
per episode. She also owns a percentage of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:03.680
show's equity, allowing her to generate even&nbsp;
more income on top of her base salary. All told,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:09.440
Cuoco's net worth is reportedly more than $100&nbsp;
million. Considering that she's moved on to other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:14.320
successful projects since Big Bang ended, it&nbsp;
seems like the sky's the limit for Kaley Cuoco.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:19.280
Sean Astin has worn a lot of different&nbsp;
hats throughout his acting career.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:24.880
He's probably best known for his turn in The Lord&nbsp;
of the Rings trilogy as Samwise Gamgee, Frodo's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:30.480
stalwart traveling companion and a hero in his own&nbsp;
right. But you've probably seen him in plenty of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:35.680
other things since then. Stranger Things, No Good&nbsp;
Nick, and Supergirl are just a few of the credits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:40.640
he's racked up since leaving Middle-earth. He also&nbsp;
has an impressive number of voiceover credits.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:46.560
Astin's first star turn came when he was only&nbsp;
13 years old when he played Mikey in the 1985&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:51.680
adventure flick The Goonies. He went on to find&nbsp;
plenty more success in the years to come in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:56.880
likes of such films as Rudy, 50 First Dates,&nbsp;
and many more. This versatility has paid off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:01.520
in a big way, as his net worth is reported&nbsp;
to be around $30 million. We're betting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:06.400
that number will only continue to grow as he&nbsp;
keeps busy with a wide variety of projects.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:12.640
Hilary Duff's childhood role remains her most&nbsp;
iconic. That's no surprise, as Lizzie McGuire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:17.680
paved the way for the many teen-centric Disney&nbsp;
Channel sitcoms that followed in its wake.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:23.200
Without Lizzie, there would surely be no Wizards&nbsp;
of Waverly Place or That's So Raven. Lizzie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:27.760
McGuire's success was thanks to many different&nbsp;
qualities, including its thoughtful writing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:32.160
and directing style, but none of it would've&nbsp;
worked without Duff's charming lead performance.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:36.400
Duff has gone on to leverage that&nbsp;
early success into a steady career,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.000
as she's starred in the likes of&nbsp;
such movies as Cheaper by the Dozen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.920
and A Cinderella Story. She's&nbsp;
also had a notable music career,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:49.440
as she's notched some chart-topping singles and&nbsp;
sold millions of albums. On top of all that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:53.920
she's branched out into a number of different&nbsp;
fashion and lifestyle brands as she continues&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:59.440
to be a force in movies and TV. Her most recent&nbsp;
notable credit is surely Kelsey Peters, a book&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:05.600
editor on the TV Land series Younger. Overall, her&nbsp;
net worth is estimated to be around $25 million.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:11.440
Unlike a lot of former child stars,&nbsp;
Reese Witherspoon didn't really have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:16.720
one massive role that broke her into the public&nbsp;
consciousness. Instead, she worked steadily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:21.600
finding a lot of success as a teenager, then&nbsp;
capably handling things as she rose through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:27.200
ranks to genuine superstardom. Nowadays, you could&nbsp;
pretty easily argue that she's one of the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:32.640
bankable stars in the world, and her estimated&nbsp;
net worth of over $200 million reflects that.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:37.040
Witherspoon's first major part came at the&nbsp;
age of 14, when she landed the lead in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.840
coming-of-age film The Man in the Moon. Then&nbsp;
she really hit the big time in the late 90s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:47.520
and early 2000s with such hit movies as Cruel&nbsp;
Intentions, Election, and Legally Blonde. She's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:53.040
also branched out to TV in a big way, with&nbsp;
Big Little Lies and Little Fires Everywhere.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:58.320
Much of Witherspoon's recent success also stems&nbsp;
from her work behind the scenes, as she frequently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:04.080
produces the projects she acts in, thereby giving&nbsp;
herself an enviable amount of quality control. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:08.240
sure seems poised to continue her domination over&nbsp;
the entertainment industry in the years to come.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:14.320
Nowadays, Ron Howard is better known for his work&nbsp;
behind the camera. He won a Directing Oscar for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:19.520
A Beautiful Mind, and he's helmed plenty of&nbsp;
other notable films like Apollo 13 and Solo:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:23.920
A Star Wars Story. But he actually&nbsp;
got his start in Hollywood as a child&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:27.840
actor. He started performing when he was&nbsp;
just five years old, and when he was six,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:33.520
he landed the breakout iconic role of Opie Taylor&nbsp;
on The Andy Griffith Show. He enjoyed further&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:38.160
acting success as a teenager and young adult,&nbsp;
thanks especially to the George Lucas-directed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:42.880
American Graffiti and the nostalgia-heavy&nbsp;
sitcom Happy Days. Howard still appears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:47.680
occasionally on screen, and he also delivered&nbsp;
some iconic voice work on Arrested Development.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.280
"Hey, that's the name of the show."

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:54.400
Ultimately, Howard has garnered most of his&nbsp;
fame and fortune as a director and producer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:57.360
His net worth is estimated&nbsp;
to be around $200 million.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:01.520
That's a truly whopping number, but&nbsp;
it's pretty much what you'd expect from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:05.760
someone who's equally comfortable directing&nbsp;
historical dramas as the latest Star War.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:11.920
Drew Barrymore's experiences as a child actor&nbsp;
are both legendary and infamous. She started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:16.880
performing at a very early age, with her first&nbsp;
big role coming when she was only seven in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:23.040
massively successful E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial.&nbsp;
That movie turned her into an overnight sensation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:28.480
She continued to land big parts, but she also&nbsp;
fell into the deepest depths of Hollywood's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:33.840
party culture before she was even a teenager.&nbsp;
She was introduced to drugs and alcohol at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:38.400
the age most kids are busy learning long&nbsp;
division. When she was just 16 years old,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:43.440
she wrote an autobiography called Little Girl&nbsp;
Lost that details her struggles with addiction.

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:48.480
Luckily, Barrymore was able to recover from that&nbsp;
trauma and go on to have a lengthy and vibrant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:53.520
career. She's appeared in a number of films&nbsp;
alongside her good buddy Adam Sandler, headlined&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:58.240
the Charlie's Angels flicks, and now she's&nbsp;
hosting her own talk show. She also has her own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:03.200
production company, and she's even tried her hand&nbsp;
at directing. She's had her ups and downs, but she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:09.120
ultimately ended up doing quite well for herself,&nbsp;
as she has an estimated net worth of $125 million.

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:12.080
"Um, freaking out!"

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.400
Jodie Foster has been a major&nbsp;
player in Hollywood for decades,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:19.840
so it can be easy to forget that&nbsp;
she got started at a very young age.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:26.240
Indeed, she was only six years old when she first&nbsp;
appeared on screen. She made a big impression on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:31.360
Martin Scorsese when she appeared in his&nbsp;
1974 film Alice Doesn't Live Here Anymore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:37.600
which led to her big break a couple of years later&nbsp;
in his iconic 1976 flick Taxi Driver. She nabbed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:43.200
an Oscar nomination for that film at just 14&nbsp;
years old — a hard feat to top, you might assume.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:48.880
But the indefatigable Foster climbed to an even&nbsp;
higher level of stardom in 1991, when she starred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:54.160
as FBI trainee Clarice Starling in The Silence&nbsp;
of the Lambs and won the Oscar for Lead Actress.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:59.040
At this particular peak of her fame, Foster&nbsp;
negotiated massive salaries for herself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:03.760
as she went on to make big bucks for the&nbsp;
likes of Contact, Panic Room, and Flightplan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:08.400
She still appears on screen occasionally, but she&nbsp;
seems to be focusing more on her work behind the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:13.600
camera at this stage in her career. She's directed&nbsp;
a few films, as well as episodes of TV shows like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:18.800
Orange is the New Black and Black Mirror. Her&nbsp;
net worth is estimated to be over $100 million,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:23.280
and she has the extremely impressive&nbsp;
filmography to prove that she deserves it.

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:28.160
Christian Bale is one of the biggest stars&nbsp;
in Hollywood. His major breakthrough came&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:33.200
in his mid-20s when he starred in the 2000&nbsp;
attention-grabbing thriller American Psycho.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:38.080
But he'd been bit by the Hollywood bug long before&nbsp;
his bloody turn as Patrick Bateman. His first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:43.600
major role came when he was just 13 in the Steven&nbsp;
Spielberg-directed war drama Empire of the Sun.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:48.800
Soon after, he went on to star in the likes of&nbsp;
Newsies and the 1994 version of Little Women.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:52.560
Thus, it's no stretch to say that Bale&nbsp;
was already a major name in Hollywood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:58.080
when he achieved true superstar status&nbsp;
with 2005's Batman Begins. Since then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:03.120
Bale has been a bonafide A-lister, appearing&nbsp;
in blockbusters and arthouse films alike.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:07.200
He's developed a reputation for undergoing&nbsp;
massive physical transformations to look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:11.680
the part for his various roles, and he's&nbsp;
received dozens of accolades along the way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:17.120
including an Oscar for 2010's The Fighter. He's&nbsp;
also negotiated some massive salaries over his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:23.120
career, and he's still going strong. He has a&nbsp;
net worth estimated to be around $125 million,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:28.560
and as he continues to land roles in more major&nbsp;
franchises, that number will surely only go up.

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:29.804
"Abracadabra."

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:34.800
It's easy to lose track of just how&nbsp;
massive some pop stars truly are,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:40.160
so it can be difficult to understand exactly how&nbsp;
high Ariana Grande's perch at the very top of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:45.520
fame ladder really is. When she was just 15,&nbsp;
she hit the stage in the Broadway musical 13,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:48.960
and she ended up dropping out of high&nbsp;
school to focus on her music career.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:53.360
She went on to reach a truly massive audience&nbsp;
when she was cast in the Nickelodeon sitcom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:58.640
Victorious and then went on to also star&nbsp;
in the spinoff Sam &amp; Cat. Her success as an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:04.400
actor is nothing to sneeze at, but her bread and&nbsp;
butter has very much turned out to be pop music,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:09.280
as she's achieved stratospheric heights of&nbsp;
popularity while putting out chart-topping tunes.

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:13.360
Grande has been making bank for a while&nbsp;
now, reportedly earning somewhere between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:19.040
$20 and $30 million per year at the height of her&nbsp;
fame, and those numbers only continue to grow.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:24.320
She reportedly earned more than $70&nbsp;
million from June 2019 through June 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:27.920
an absolutely astounding figure&nbsp;
for someone in her mid-20s.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:32.960
Grande's most recent albums and concert tours have&nbsp;
attracted even bigger crowds and ticket sales.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:37.200
It will be interesting to see just how&nbsp;
long she can keep her winning streak alive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:41.760
Based on how she's been going so far, we don't&nbsp;
expect her to start slowing down any time soon.

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:46.720
It can be easy to forget just how&nbsp;
prolific Neil Patrick Harris truly is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:51.120
He's shown off a wide array of talents over&nbsp;
the years on both the big and small screens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:55.360
as well as on the Broadway stage. His&nbsp;
biggest claims to fame are probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:59.360
his TV roles, but theater fans can&nbsp;
certainly claim him as their own.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:04.640
You don't get to host the Tony Awards four times&nbsp;
if you're not a Broadway superstar, after all.

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:09.200
As Harris has gone through a few career&nbsp;
reinventions, it can be easy to forget how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:14.640
he started. He started acting as a teenager in&nbsp;
the late 80s, and he was 16 when he landed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:20.560
lead role on Doogie Howser, M.D. After that show&nbsp;
ended, he continued to act consistently throughout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:25.760
the 90s, but it wasn't until 2005 when he returned&nbsp;
to the heights of superstardom as he took on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:30.560
role of the womanizing Barney Stinson on How&nbsp;
I Met Your Mother, which ended up earning him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:35.920
four Emmy nominations. Considering his charisma,&nbsp;
talent, and general likeability, we expect that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:40.080
Harris will continue to remain relevant for&nbsp;
the foreseeable future. He's certainly done&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:46.400
well so far, as he has an estimated net worth&nbsp;
of around $50 million. Nice work, Doogie!

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:47.600
"It's gonna be legendary!"

